    "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. For q-71048, the direction vector is (7,-3,0), so z=6 is a separate constraint. For q-71030, subtract the point coordinates and divide by the direction components (4,-5,3). For q-127527, Q-P=(2,-2,0), giving the symmetric equation with z=3. For q-110307, f^{-1}(4)=-3 and the product rule gives 1(-3)+3/5=-12/5. For q-110497, f^{-1}(8)=2 and f'(2)=9 ln(3), so the inverse derivative is its reciprocal. For q-75986, the domain is x>4, f^{-1}(0)=5, and f'(5)=5, giving 1/5; the source's candidate x=0 is outside the domain and is explicitly discarded. For the plane questions, a normal vector n gives n·r=n·P. The constants are -21 for q-32971 and -11 for q-70647. Parallel vectors must be orthogonal to the plane normal: 6a-2b=0 gives a/b=1/3 for q-33319, and -5a-b=0 gives a/b=-1/5 for q-70822. For q-70892, B-A=(1,1,1) and its dot product with Q is 2. For q-33317, B-A=(-1,5,-1) and its dot product with Q is -23. The remaining normal vectors and point dot products give 2x+4y-z=13, x+y+3z=-6, 3x-5y+2z=-1, and 4y+z=4, respectively. Each selected token comes from the current choices. Confirmation rests on captured worked solutions; no grading evidence was supplied.",
